                "word": "euphuism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f1e99ed8-ffd3-4b37-8c59-731eb399516f",
                        "entry_id": "db559199-2ddf-3b09-99ed-d4e8e61fd646",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "euphuisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f074eb3e-0a39-35d6-a774-dc926d9a7a3e",
                        "entry_id": "db559199-2ddf-3b09-99ed-d4e8e61fd646",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ornate style of writing (in Elizabethan England) marked by the excessive use of alliteration, antithesis and mythological similes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aee208cb-fcfc-3725-afd3-46075c21e5fb",
                        "entry_id": "db559199-2ddf-3b09-99ed-d4e8e61fd646",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An instance of euphuism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e20cf672-733b-4964-9709-c85e8a96bba3",
                                "sense_id": "aee208cb-fcfc-3725-afd3-46075c21e5fb",
                                "text": "I have not the slightest faith in Carlyle. In ten years–possibly in five–he will be remembered only as a butt for sarcasm. His linguistic Euphuisms might very well have been taken as prima facie evidence of his philosophic ones; they were the froth which indicated, first, the shallowness, and secondly, the confusion of the waters."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18fddc3f-3d68-47da-9823-1efab269dd07",
                                "sense_id": "aee208cb-fcfc-3725-afd3-46075c21e5fb",
                                "text": "“Generalstaatsverordnetenversammlungen” seems to be “Generalstatesrepresentativesmeetings,” as nearly as I can get at it,—a mere rhythmical, gushy euphuism for “meetings of the legislature,” I judge."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6c9c0ae-24db-4878-8869-231609ed85cb",
                        "source_entry_id": "db559199-2ddf-3b09-99ed-d4e8e61fd646",
                        "source_sense_description": "style of writing",
                        "target_lang_word": "euphuisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "euphuisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1258ef8b-6170-3aaa-8144-b8fcd33ab914",
                                        "entry_id": "e44f4189-a85a-344a-a530-196803334b8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Style précieux qui était à la mode en Angleterre à la cour d’Élisabeth Iʳᵉ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cb927c0-b296-416e-9951-6aa460eb7770",
                                                "sense_id": "1258ef8b-6170-3aaa-8144-b8fcd33ab914",
                                                "text": "Le faux esprit régnait alors presque partout, – en Angleterre en Italie, en Espagne, en France, – sous différents noms. En Italie, c’étaient les concetti, ou le Marinisme ; en Espagne, les conceptos, ou agudezas (les pointes), ou le Gongorisme, ou le cultisme ; en Angleterre, l’euphuïsme ; en France, l’esprit précieux."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bf73512-167a-374e-b8b2-3817300eecd3",
                                        "entry_id": "e44f4189-a85a-344a-a530-196803334b8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Style affecté."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e584da5d-af28-4349-861a-0499fee8527c",
                                                "sense_id": "5bf73512-167a-374e-b8b2-3817300eecd3",
                                                "text": "Plût à Dieu ! madame, nous ne serions pas obligés, quelques beaux esprits de mes amis et moi, de réveiller dans cette pauvre France, engourdie aux bas-fonds de la vulgarité roturière, la politesse des siècles monarchiques et chrétiens, la prudhomie du goût, les grâces de l’euphuisme et les allures fringantes du style gentilhomme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c61f5ec-20ae-48d3-9dbd-82bfecfaf7a9",
                                                "sense_id": "5bf73512-167a-374e-b8b2-3817300eecd3",
                                                "text": "Ces mots s’appellent les uns les autres, éveillés par la consonance, et, sur ces sonorités, ils rebondissent en se multipliant. Ce sont les arabesques de style, les préciosités, les mignardises, l’euphuisme des époques entêtées de recherches."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aeff520d-7319-4983-b676-e567f85110d5",
                        "source_entry_id": "db559199-2ddf-3b09-99ed-d4e8e61fd646",
